# ───────── Design mockups ─────────
# The APPROVED SHEETS — `docs/design/src/0X-*.html` — are the project's design
# specification and are COMMITTED. They were ignored here as "intermediate build output"
# while the PNG renders were kept as "the reviewed artefact", and that was backwards in
# a way that cost the dashboard most of its design:
#
#   A PNG carries style — colour, radius, spacing, weight. It cannot carry structure:
#   that a table has eight columns named «الطلب … الحالة», that a header pairs «تصدير
#   CSV» with «دعوة كابتن», that four named cards sit above a queue. So "match the
#   design" degraded into reading a picture and inferring, and `scripts/check-design-
#   parity.mjs` measured the result at 31 of 103 required elements — while every other
#   gate passed, because they all compared the code to itself.
#
# The sheets are text. Text can be diffed, grepped, reviewed in a PR, and gated in CI.
# They stay in the repository.
#
# Only the throwaway render scaffolding is ignored: `r-*.html` are single-poster wrappers
# that `gen-*.mjs` writes and `shoot.mjs` immediately screenshots, and `build/` holds the
# marketing card intermediates.
docs/design/src/r-*.html
docs/design/src/build/
docs/design/src/_mkt-index.json
